Lucas Brutschy created KAFKA-19945:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: StreamsGroupHearbeat response should always set the s=
tatus
                 Key: KAFKA-19945
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19945
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
    Affects Versions: 4.2.0
            Reporter: Lucas Brutschy


The status field should always set in the response, even when empty, to ens=
ure that the status gets reset on the client.

We are not doing this due to an oversight - it is defined as nullable, and =
is null when not set. So status does not clear correctly on the client, whi=
ch ignores the field if it's null.=C2=A0

This mostly has no effect, since we are logging the status, but it is still=
 confusing.



