>
> Regarding the missing sub-menus and navigation structure, I'd like to
> clarify the design approach taken with the new Hugo-based site, which
> aligns with what is documented in the KIP-1133 (
>
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=3D340036=
497#KIP1133:AKDocumentationandWebsiteinMarkdown-AKversionspecificdocumentat=
ion
> )
>
>
> 1. Content Organization & Navigation: Unlike the original website, the ne=
w
> source is organized into modular sections. Large, monolithic pages
> (like `ops.html` or `configuration.html`) have been split into smaller,
> more manageable pages.
>
> - Left Sidebar:Automatically displays these sections and pages as the
> primary navigation menu.
> - Right Sidebar (TOC): Displays the headings (H2, H3, etc.) within the
> current page.
>
> 2. Why not merge TOC into the Left Sidebar? I explored integrating the TO=
C
> headings directly into the left sidebar menu to mimic the previous
> "sub-menu" feel. However, this resulted in an excessively deep hierarchy
> that became cluttered and difficult to navigate. It also proved technical=
ly
> challenging to apply selectively to only certain sections without
> complicating the build logic.
>
> Instead of a deep nested menu, I've implemented a hybrid navigation (with
> left sidebar and right toc navbar) system to make finding content easier:
>
> Further, I added the following enhancements:
>
> - Sticky & Seamless Scrolling: Both the Left Sidebar and Right TOC are no=
w
> sticky. They scroll seamlessly with the main content but can also be
> scrolled independently.
> - Smart Scrollspy: Right TOC automatically highlights the current locatio=
n.
> If the user is viewing a deep subheading (e.g., H4) that isn't in the TOC=
,
> it intelligently highlights the parent section so that context is
> preserved=3D
> .
> - Offline Search: fast, local search (using Lunr.js) that indexes the
> latest documentation. This makes finding specific details instantaneous,
> often faster than navigating a complex menu.
> - Powered By Page: I have updated the "Powered By" page to match the
> spacing, width, and order of the cards as you suggested.
>
> Here is a gif showing this in action:
> https://gist.github.com/hvishwanath/461fd54c792b84fd23bbc952560b9235
>
>
> The latest changes are live at https://kafka.staged.apache.org/. I believ=
e
> this combination of structured page navigation, context-aware TOC, and fa=
st
> search provides strong support for navigation and offers a good user
> experience.
>
> Thanks again for all your review, feedback and suggestions. Looking forwa=
rd
> to starting the vote thread soon.
>
> Regards,
> Harish
>
