Subject: Re: [DISCUSS] AlterConfigPolicy behavior in 3.9.2
Date: Fri, 5 Dec 2025 07:33:09 +0800
Message-Id: <963A3471-BAFC-4603-BCA9-FA0982DB1860@gmail.com>
References: <CAN64TSmZ5vrtUws4VDUhRJXb5A1r90gyfm6RCqVLTBskmFMTzA@mail.gmail.com>
In-Reply-To: <CAN64TSmZ5vrtUws4VDUhRJXb5A1r90gyfm6RCqVLTBskmFMTzA@mail.gmail.com>
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
X-Mailer: iPhone Mail (23A341)
From: Chia-Ping Tsai <chia7712@gmail.com>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>
Cc: dev@kafka.apache.org

How about introducing a configuration called alter.config.policy.kraft.compa=
tibility.enable to control this behavior?

The default value would be false, meaning nothing changes in 3.9.2. Converse=
ly, setting it to true would align the behavior with KRaft policy validation=
=20

> Edoardo Comar <edoardlists@gmail.com> =E6=96=BC 2025=E5=B9=B412=E6=9C=884=E6=
=97=A5 =E6=99=9A=E4=B8=8A10:15 =E5=AF=AB=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A
>=20
> =EF=BB=BFChia-Ping,
> I respectfully disagree with such a quick decision.
>=20
>> On Thu, 4 Dec 2025 at 02:07, Chia-Ping Tsai <chia7712@gmail.com> wrote:
>>=20
>> Long-standing bugs often become features.
>>=20
>> Let's keep this behavior for 3.9.2. I recommend updating the documentatio=
n
>> to explicitly highlight this distinction.
>>=20
>>=20
>> Ismael Juma <me@ismaeljuma.com> =E6=96=BC 2025=E5=B9=B412=E6=9C=884=E6=97=
=A5=E9=80=B1=E5=9B=9B =E4=B8=8A=E5=8D=886:23=E5=AF=AB=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A
>>=20
>>> Thanks for starting the discussion. Given that this behavior has existed=

>>> for so long, I would be reluctant to change it in a patch release for 3.=
9.x
>>> unless there is strong demand from the community.
>>>=20
>>> Ismael
>>>=20
>>>> On Mon, Dec 1, 2025 at 6:18=E2=80=AFAM PoAn Yang <yangpoan@gmail.com> w=
rote:
>>>=20
>>>> Hi developers,
>>>>=20
>>>> I'd like to initiate a discussion regarding the AlterConfigPolicy in
>>>> version 3.9.2.
>>>> https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19026
>>>>=20
>>>> The key issue is the difference in behavior for OpType.SUBTRACT and
>>>> OpType.APPEND between KRaft and ZK modes.
>>>>=20
>>>> In KRaft mode, AlterConfigPolicy#validate receives the modified
>>>> RequestMetadata.
>>>> In ZK mode, it receives the original user input.
>>>>=20
>>>> We can observe this difference by looking at the OpType.SUBTRACT exampl=
e
>>>> provided in the attachments:
>>>>=20
>>>>=20
>>> https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13075589/KAFKA19026Test=
.java
>>>>=20
>>>>=20
>>> https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13075585/KAFKA19026Poli=
cy.java
>>>>=20
>>>> Example Output in KRaft Mode:
>>>> AlterConfigPolicy.RequestMetadata(resource=3DConfigResource(type=3DBROK=
ER,
>>>> name=3D'0'), configs=3D{ssl.cipher.suites=3D}).
>>>>=20
>>>> Example Output in ZK Mode:
>>>> AlterConfigPolicy.RequestMetadata(resource=3DConfigResource(type=3DBROK=
ER,
>>>> name=3D'0'), configs=3D{ssl.cipher.suites=3Dfoo}).
>>>>=20
>>>> The ZK behavior has been in place since 2.3.1. Therefore, I want to che=
ck
>>>> if the community wants to align this behavior in 3.9.2.
>>>>=20
>>>>=20
>>>>=20
>>> https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/2.3.1/core/src/main/scala/kafka/ser=
ver/AdminManager.scala#L462-L479
>>>>=20
>>>> If this is considered a behavioral change, it might be risky to include=

>>> in
>>>> a patch version (3.9.2). However, if it's classified as a bug, then we
>>>> should proceed with the fix in 3.9.2.
>>>>=20
>>>> Feel free to share your opinions. Thank you!
>>>>=20
>>>> Best regards,
>>>> PoAn
>>>=20

