Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-19967) Reduce GC pressure in tiered storage
 read path by using direct memory buffers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Nandini Singhal (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Nandini Singhal created KAFKA-19967:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: Reduce GC pressure in tiered storage read path by usi=
ng direct memory buffers
                 Key: KAFKA-19967
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19967
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: Tiered-Storage
            Reporter: Nandini Singhal


Large heap buffer allocations in the tiered storage read path cause signifi=
cant GC pressure by creating "humongous" objects that bypass young generati=
on and go directly to old generation. Using direct buffers for these I/O-ce=
ntric allocations would eliminate this GC overhead.

(RemoteLogManager.java:1718):
{code:java}
=C2=A0 int updatedFetchSize =3D remoteStorageFetchInfo.minOneMessage() && f=
irstBatchSize > maxBytes
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 ? firstBatchSize
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 : maxBytes;
=C2=A0 ByteBuffer buffer =3D ByteBuffer.allocate(updatedFetchSize);{code}
=C2=A0 Where maxBytes =3D Math.min(fetchMaxBytes, fetchInfo.maxBytes), whic=
h can be configured up to 55MB or
=C2=A0 more depending on:
=C2=A0 - replica.fetch.max.bytes (default: 1MB)
=C2=A0 - replica.fetch.response.max.bytes (default: 10MB)
=C2=A0 - Client-side max.partition.fetch.bytes

=C2=A0

In the G1GC collector (Kafka's default), objects larger than half a region =
size (~32MB with 64MB regions) are considered "humongous" and:
=C2=A0 1. Skip eden and young generation entirely
=C2=A0 2. Allocated directly in old generation
=C2=A0 3. Can only be reclaimed during expensive full/mixed GCs
=C2=A0 4. Trigger old GCs more frequently

=C2=A0 Example: With a 4GB heap and InitiatingHeapOccupancyPercent=3D35, ap=
proximately 25 concurrent tiered storage fetch requests (25 =C3=97 55MB =3D=
 1.375GB) would trigger an old GC. Under high read load from tiered storage=
, this creates continuous GC pressure.

=C2=A0



