Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-19968) Tiered Storage Fetch Quotas Not
 Enforced - Quota Check Does Not Account for In-Flight Fetch Size
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Nandini Singhal (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Nandini Singhal created KAFKA-19968:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: Tiered Storage Fetch Quotas Not Enforced - Quota Chec=
k Does Not Account for In-Flight Fetch Size
                 Key: KAFKA-19968
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19968
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: Tiered-Storage
            Reporter: Nandini Singhal


Tiered storage fetch quotas are not properly enforced. Brokers can signific=
antly exceed configured fetch quota limits because the quota check only eva=
luates historical usage and does not account for the size of the fetch requ=
est that is=C2=A0about to be executed.

The issues are:
 # Quota check happens BEFORE the fetch
 # The check only considers past usage
 # The fetch size is known but not considered
 # Actual bytes are recorded AFTER the fetch completes

Example Scenario:

=C2=A0 - Configured quota: 136 MB/s
=C2=A0 - Current usage (past 1 second window): 100 MB/s
=C2=A0 - New fetch request arrives requesting 50 MB

=C2=A0 Current behavior:
=C2=A0 1. getFetchThrottleTimeMs() checks: 100 MB/s < 136 MB/s =E2=86=92 No=
t violated, returns 0
=C2=A0 2. Fetch proceeds and downloads 50 MB
=C2=A0 3. Total throughput: 150 MB/s =E2=86=92 Exceeds quota by 14 MB/s
=C2=A0 4. quotaManager.record(50 MB) is called
=C2=A0 5. Next request will be throttled, but quota has already been exceed=
ed



