Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-19970) Add time-based eviction to tiered
 storage index cache to prevent stale entries from accumulating
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Nandini Singhal (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Nandini Singhal created KAFKA-19970:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: Add time-based eviction to tiered storage index cache=
 to prevent stale entries from accumulating
                 Key: KAFKA-19970
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19970
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: Tiered-Storage
            Reporter: Nandini Singhal


The remote log index cache (RemoteIndexCache) currently only uses weight-ba=
sed eviction. This can cause old, smaller index files to remain cached inde=
finitely while newer indices thrash the cache, leading=C2=A0to inefficient =
cache utilization and increased remote fetch failures.

(RemoteIndexCache.java:142-144):
{code:java}
=C2=A0 return Caffeine.newBuilder()
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .maximumWeight(maxSize)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .weigher((Uuid key, Entry entry) -> (int=
) entry.entrySizeBytes)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .evictionListener(...)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 .build();{code}
=C2=A0 In environments with:
=C2=A0 - Heavy backfill workloads (reading old data once, then moving to ne=
wer data)
=C2=A0 - Sequential read patterns through tiered storage
=C2=A0 - Variable index file sizes

=C2=A0 The cache can end up in a state where:
=C2=A0 - Old index files from completed backfills remain cached (small, low=
 frequency)
=C2=A0 - Newer index files thrash continuously (larger, similar frequency)
=C2=A0 - Cache hit rate degrades over time
=C2=A0 - Increased remote storage fetch errors due to cache misses

=C2=A0

Add time-based eviction using Caffeine's expireAfterAccess to the cache con=
figuration so that even if an entry remains in a favorable frequency bucket=
, it will be evicted after=C2=A0not being accessed for the configured durat=
ion.



