Hi all,

Following the community review, I would like to call for a vote on cutting
over to markdown based AK website (KIP 1133). Fully functional site is live
on staging at https://kafka.staged.apache.org/.

If the Vote Passes:

- I will migrate the source documentation in the docs directory of the
apache/kafka repository to Markdown for versions *3.5 and newer.*
- Older versions (pre-3.5) will be left as-is (HTML) in the kafka repo to
avoid disruption.
- Update CI/CD deploy the markdown branch to the live production site.

For reference:

- KIP 1133:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1133%3A+AK+Documentation+and+Website+in+Markdown#KIP1133:AKDocumentationandWebsiteinMarkdown-AKwebsitedocumentation
- Previous discussions:
https://lists.apache.org/thread/yr5rqyx1d6lvyb9t9tbf26stsh214v4r
- Markdown source for AK website: `markdown` branch at
https://github.com/apache/kafka-site

Regards,
Harish

