Kirk True resolved KAFKA-18217.
-------------------------------
    Resolution: Cannot Reproduce

We've done several experiments and tests and have not found any evidence th=
at this is a problem. There have been several performance-related changes t=
o the AsyncKafkaConsumer in the last 9 months or so, thus it's possible it =
was addressed then. Please reopen if there's another occurrence. Thanks

> Slow HWM/LSO update might have subtle effect on the consumer lag reportin=
g
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
-
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-18217
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18217
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>          Components: clients, consumer
>            Reporter: Philip Nee
>            Assignee: Evan Zhou
>            Priority: Minor
>              Labels: async-kafka-consumer-performance, consumer-threading=
-refactor, performance
>             Fix For: 4.2.0
>
>
> We've discovered the consumer lag metrics appear spiky for the AsyncKafka=
Consumer.=C2=A0 We examined how HWM/LSO is updated and measure the cadence =
between the two consumer using the local examples. TL;DR - Consumer Lag met=
rics can sometimes be off due to KAFKA-18216 and slowness of HWM/LSO update=
.
> =C2=A0
> Context: Fetcher performs multiple consumer lag measurements between two =
HWM/LSO updates.=C2=A0 The closer the HWM/LSO update, the better the lag me=
asurement is because
> lag =3D HWM/LSO - fetch position
> The elementary statics show the behavioral differences between the 2 cons=
umer implementations.=C2=A0 The data will vary based on the platform runnin=
g these tests, so this is just for the reader's reference. (These are the o=
utputs of my custom script).=C2=A0 Both are measuring by produce-consuming =
200 million records.
> =C2=A0
> AsyncKafkaConsumer
> Updating 7179 HWM/LSO
> Average HWM/LSO increment: 3589.99
> Standard deviation of increment: 2381.07
> Average number of 'recording lag' count: 7.69
> Standard deviation of 'recording lag' count: 4.66
> =C2=A0
> ClassicKafkaConsumer
> Updating 58418 HWM/LSO
> Average HWM/LSO increment 1223.02
> Standard deviation of increment: 532.52
> Average 'recording lag' count: 2.95
> Standard deviation of 'recording lag' count: 1.10



