@@ -1249,7 +1249,9 @@ <h4 class="anchor-heading"><a id="prodconfig" class="anchor-link"></a><a href="#
 
   <h3 class="anchor-heading"><a id="java" class="anchor-link"></a><a href="#java">6.6 Java Version</a></h3>
 
-  Java 8, Java 11, Java 17, Java 21 and Java 23 are supported.
+  Java 8, 11, 17, 21, and 23 are fully supported while Java 25 is supported for unit and integration tests only.

Review Comment:
   My point is that JDK 23 can be used for both compilation and testing. In contrast, JDK 25 is used only for running tests, which minimizes necessary changes. This means JDK 23 works with all our Gradle tasks, while JDK 25 is limited to the special test task, `testWithJava25`



