    Resolution: Fixed

> Introduce a new config for group coordinator max record size
> ------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-19519
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19519
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>            Reporter: Luke Chen
>            Assignee: Lan Ding
>            Priority: Major
>              Labels: need-kip
>             Fix For: 4.3.0
>
>
> In=C2=A0KAFKA-19427, there's a use case that when there is a consumer gro=
up subscribes huge amount of topics/partitions, when this group is rebalanc=
ed, and then the coordinator broker stores the assignment of this group to =
__consumer_offsets, it will throw an error RecordTooLargeException .
> =C2=A0
> =C2=A0
> =C2=A0
> Currently, to resolve this issue, the only solution is to increase the br=
oker-level `message.max.bytes` config. But the side effect of this change i=
s it potentially allows all topics without override the topic level \{{max.=
message.bytes}} config, will now allow higher message size.
> =C2=A0
> =C2=A0
> =C2=A0
> We could introduce a new config to drive the value used by the group coor=
dinator - e.g group.coordinator.append.max.bytes - instead of relying on th=
e broker message.max.bytes. This would be used to set the max bytes at the =
topic level when the topic is created.



