Jun Rao created KAFKA-20003:
-------------------------------

             Summary: Buffer released too early in MemoryPool
                 Key: KAFKA-20003
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20003
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
    Affects Versions: 4.1.1, 4.0.1, 3.9.1, 3.8.1, 3.7.2, 3.6.2, 3.5.2, 3.4.=
1, 3.3.2, 3.3.0, 3.2.3, 3.1.2, 3.0.2, 2.8.2, 2.7.2
            Reporter: Jun Rao
             Fix For: 4.2.0


https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-10386 we introduced Type.COMPAC=
T_RECORDS in SchemaGenerator. However, we forgot to add Type.COMPACT_RECORD=
S to ApiKeys.retainsBufferReference(). This can cause the buffer in MemoryP=
ool to be released too early, leading the data corruption and potential oth=
er weird problems.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

This issue is already fixed via https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA=
-19634, but the changes are large. We probably should just fix the issue in=
 ApiKeys.retainsBufferReference() in 4.2.0 and earlier versions.



