Hi all,

Thank you to everyone who provided feedback on this proposal.

Our primary motivation for KIP-1176 is to significantly reduce the
operational cost of Kafka in the cloud. While we believe KIP-1176
offers a viable solution, the parallel discussion on KIP-1150
(Diskless Topics) has presented a more comprehensive, cloud-native
architecture that solves these same problems.

To avoid splitting community focus and engineering effort, we have
decided to withdraw KIP-1176 in favor of KIP-1150.

Instead of competing, we are joining forces with the KIP-1150 team. We
will be contributing our engineering resources to the initiative to
help accelerate the delivery of the Diskless architecture. Please
direct future discussion to the KIP-1150 thread.

Thanks,
Tom & Henry (Haiying Cai)


