>> >> min.isr=3D2 for the __remote_log_metadata topic.
>> >>
>> >> KIP:
>> >>
>> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1235%3A+Correct+th=
e+default+min.insync.replicas+to+2+for+the+__remote_log_metadata+topic
>> >>
>> >> Problem:
>> >>
>> >> Currently, __remote_log_metadata relies on the broker default for
>> min.isr
>> >> (typically 1).
>> >> With min.isr=3D1 and factor=3D3, acknowledged writes can be lost if t=
he
>> leader
>> >> crashes before replication
>> >> completes, making remote data permanently unreachable.
>> >>
>> >> What's more, the similar topic: __transaction_state sets min.isr=3D2 =
via
>> >> transaction.state.log.min.isr.
>> >> We should provide the same durability for __remote_log_metadata.
>> >>
>> >>
>> >> Proposed Change:
>> >>
>> >> Add one new broker config: remote.log.metadata.topic.min.isr (default=
:
>> 2)
>> >>
>> >> When creating __remote_log_metadata, TopicBasedRemoteLogMetadataManag=
er
>> >> will set
>> >> min.insync.replicas=3D2 at the topic level. The change only affects n=
ew
>> >> clusters enabling Tiered Storage. Existing topics are unchanged.
>> >>
>> >>
>> >> Looking forward to your feedback!
>> >>
>> >> Best regards,
>> >> Jian
>> >>
>>
>>
