.1, 3.5.2, 3.6.2, 3.7.2, 3.8.1, 3.9.1, 4.0.1, 4.1.1
>            Reporter: Jun Rao
>            Assignee: =E9=BB=83=E7=AB=A3=E9=99=BD
>            Priority: Minor
>             Fix For: 4.2.0
>
>
> https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-10386 we introduced Type.COMP=
ACT_RECORDS in SchemaGenerator. However, we forgot to add Type.COMPACT_RECO=
RDS to ApiKeys.retainsBufferReference(). This can cause the buffer in Memor=
yPool to be released too early, leading the data corruption and potential o=
ther weird problems.=C2=A0
> =C2=A0
> This issue is already fixed via https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAF=
KA-19634, but the changes are large. We probably should just fix the issue =
in ApiKeys.retainsBufferReference() in 4.2.0 and earlier versions.



