Hi all,

I have updated the KIP-1247 based on feedback from Chia-Ping.

Key changes:

   - The KIP now proposes to make only the core *Bytes* methods officially
   public (*Bytes, wrap, get, compareTo, equals, hashCode, toString*)
   - Helper methods/fields (*increment(), ByteArrayComparator,
   BYTES_LEXICO_COMPARATOR*) will be moved to
"*org.apache.kafka.common.utils.internals
   package*"
   - This approach keeps the public API minimal while allowing internal
   Kafka code to continue using the helpers

Updated KIP:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1247%3A+Make+Bytes+ut=
ils+class+part+of+the+public+API

Please review the changes and let me know if you have any concerns. If
there are no objections in the next few days, then I would like to call for
a vote.

Thank you.

Best regards,
Siddhartha

