         Attachments: image-2025-12-30-16-27-52-195.png, image-2025-12-30-1=
6-28-25-539.png, image-2025-12-30-16-28-42-798.png, image-2025-12-30-16-29-=
03-343.png, image-2025-12-30-16-29-19-289.png, image-2025-12-30-16-29-36-54=
2.png

Hello=EF=BC=8CDuring my usage of Kafka, I identified an issue. In the {{kaf=
ka-server-start.bat}}=C2=A0script, there is a logic that sets different sta=
rtup parameters based on the bitness (32-bit/64-bit) of the operating syste=
m. The relevant code is as follows:
{code:java}
IF ["%KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS%"] EQU [""] (
    rem detect OS architecture
    wmic os get osarchitecture | find /i "32-bit" >nul 2>&1
    IF NOT ERRORLEVEL 1 (
        rem 32-bit OS
        set KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS=3D-Xmx512M -Xms512M
    ) ELSE (
        rem 64-bit OS
        set KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS=3D-Xmx1G -Xms1G
    )
) {code}
It first queries wmic os get osarchitecture, then determines whether the op=
erating system is 32-bit or 64-bit by checking if the result contains the s=
tring "32-bit". However, my actual tests show that this method is not relia=
ble=E2=80=94the returned results vary across Windows systems with different=
 languages and regional settings, as shown below:

=C2=A0

{*}English Windows{*}:

!image-2025-12-30-16-27-52-195.png!

{*}Chinese Windows{*}:
!image-2025-12-30-16-28-25-539.png!
{*}French Windows{*}:

!image-2025-12-30-16-28-42-798.png!

{*}German Windows{*}:

!image-2025-12-30-16-29-03-343.png!

{*}Japanese Windows{*}:

*!image-2025-12-30-16-29-19-289.png!*

{*}Older Windows XP systems{*}:

!image-2025-12-30-16-29-36-542.png!

Kafka has users across the globe, and the current approach=C2=A0{*}lacks un=
iversality{*}.



