Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Matthieu Nantern created KAFKA-20025:
----------------------------------------

             Summary: Missing dynamic SSL reconfiguration support for Kafka=
RaftClient
                 Key: KAFKA-20025
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20025
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
    Affects Versions: 4.1.1, 3.9.1
            Reporter: Matthieu Nantern


Hi,

I'd like to discuss a gap in the dynamic SSL reconfiguration support for KR=
aft mode that affects brokers connecting to the controller quorum.

In KRaft mode, when SSL certificates are renewed and dynamically reloaded v=
ia {{{}kafka-configs.sh{}}}, the KafkaRaftClient (used by brokers to fetch =
cluster metadata from controllers as "observers" per KIP-853) does not pick=
 up the new certificates.

This causes SSL handshake failures with {{CertificateExpiredException}} err=
ors, even though the reload command reports success.

=C2=A0

Error observed on broker:{{=C2=A0 =C2=A0 org.apache.kafka.common.errors.Ssl=
AuthenticationException: Failed to}}
{{process post-handshake messages}}
{{=C2=A0 =C2=A0 Caused by: javax.net.ssl.SSLHandshakeException: Received fa=
tal alert:}}
{{certificate_unknown}}

Error observed on controller:
{{=C2=A0 =C2=A0 Caused by: java.security.cert.CertificateExpiredException: =
NotAfter:}}
{{Wed Dec 17 08:28:22 UTC 2025}}

The SslChannelBuilder implements ListenerReconfigurable and supports
dynamic SSL reconfiguration. However, in KafkaRaftManager, the channel buil=
der is never registered with config.addReconfigurable().

In contrast, {{NodeToControllerChannelManager}} (and other components) corr=
ectly registers the channel builder:
NodeToControllerChannelManager.scala (trunk, lines 130-132):

{{=C2=A0 =C2=A0 channelBuilder match {}}
{{=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 case reconfigurable: Reconfigurable =3D>}}
{{config.addReconfigurable(reconfigurable)}}
{{=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 case _ =3D>}}
{{=C2=A0 =C2=A0 }}}

I checked that the issue exists in both Kafka 3.9.1 and current trunk (as
of 2025-12-17).

The only reliable workaround I found is to restart the Kafka broker when
certificates are renewed. Has anyone else encountered this, or is there a r=
eason this was intentionally left out?



